# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions for infra/. Each entry needs a documented
# reason — suppressions are decisions, not noise-silencing.

# AWS-0132: "Bucket does not encrypt data with a customer managed key."
# The web bucket holds only PUBLIC static frontend assets (HTML/JS/CSS). It is
# encrypted at rest with SSE-S3 (AES256, see aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption
# _configuration.web). A customer-managed KMS key would add cost and key
# management with no benefit for non-sensitive public content, so the CMK-specific
# rule is intentionally suppressed.
AWS-0132

# AWS-0136: "Topic encryption does not use a customer managed key."
# The SNS alarm topic is encrypted with the AWS-managed key (alias/aws/sns). It
# carries only CloudWatch alarm notifications — no sensitive data — so a
# customer-managed KMS key's cost and rotation/policy management add no value.
# Same rationale as AWS-0132.
AWS-0136
